1
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:02,380
[sighs]

2
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,130
[magical chime]

3
00:00:09,930 --> 00:00:10,720
[thud & grunt]

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:19,640
[gasps]

5
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:21,610
[grunts]

6
00:00:29,950 --> 00:00:31,450
[magical chime]

7
00:00:32,910 --> 00:00:33,740
[gasps]

8
00:00:36,330 --> 00:00:37,540
[LARA] My prince?

9
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:44,550
[♪ opening music begins]

10
00:02:09,050 --> 00:02:11,170
[♪ opening music ends]

11
00:02:12,630 --> 00:02:15,010
Why did I turn into
a mermaid again?

12
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:18,060
-What did you say?
-Only one person saw her.

13
00:02:18,430 --> 00:02:19,510
I covered it up, but-—

14
00:02:20,260 --> 00:02:22,770
And then I turned back
and had legs again.

15
00:02:23,690 --> 00:02:25,440
Who saw you turn into a mermaid?

16
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,350
[magical chime]

17
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:29,860
Apparently some guy
who looked like a prince.

18
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:30,690
What?

19
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:33,150
He only looked
like him a little bit.

20
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:35,570
Anyway, why did I
turn into a mermaid?

21
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:39,370
You changed because your
heart was deeply moved.

22
00:02:39,490 --> 00:02:40,370
[gasps]

23
00:02:41,120 --> 00:02:43,500
You must have felt the
same 200 years ago,

24
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:46,580
in that moment when
you were about to unite

25
00:02:46,710 --> 00:02:48,090
with the prince in love.

26
00:02:49,130 --> 00:02:51,250
But everything is
different this time.

27
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:54,260
Sure, of course. Maybe,
were you flustered?

28
00:02:55,130 --> 00:02:56,130
That's it.

29
00:02:56,680 --> 00:02:59,100
In any case, there must
be a significant reason.

30
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:01,640
You can't rule out the
possibility that he's

31
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:04,180
the one with whom
you'll find true love.

32
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:10,610
I just got scared when
I saw his familiar face.

33
00:03:11,110 --> 00:03:12,780
He's not the one
I'm destined for.

34
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:15,070
[gasps]

35
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,280
[gasps]

36
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,240
-Here.
-Huh?

37
00:03:27,370 --> 00:03:29,000
My clothes are in here.

38
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:30,920
That day,

39
00:03:31,500 --> 00:03:33,000
when you dove into Lake Biwa

40
00:03:33,670 --> 00:03:35,550
and just left without
coming back.

41
00:03:36,470 --> 00:03:38,050
You dove into Lake Biwa?

42
00:03:38,430 --> 00:03:40,050
Also, who is this person?

43
00:03:40,550 --> 00:03:42,430
Beats me. I thought
he was a customer.

44
00:03:43,010 --> 00:03:44,600
Um, well, thank you.

45
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:47,560
I'm Luca.

46
00:03:48,310 --> 00:03:49,400
Hmm?

47
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,110
I'm... Luca.

48
00:03:51,480 --> 00:03:52,480
Yeah.

49
00:03:53,440 --> 00:03:55,190
-Your name, please?
-Huh?

50
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:56,690
Lara.

51
00:03:57,240 --> 00:03:58,200
Oh.

52
00:03:58,490 --> 00:04:00,740
[♪ cheerful music]

53
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:05,160
Does everyone know
you're a mermaid?

54
00:04:05,290 --> 00:04:07,500
Ah! No, and don't tell anyone!

55
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:10,670
Of course I won't. People
would think that was weird.

56
00:04:11,960 --> 00:04:14,050
Okay, give me your contact info.

57
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,010
Contact info?

58
00:04:17,550 --> 00:04:19,430
I don't have any contact infos.

59
00:04:19,550 --> 00:04:20,720
-Huh?
-Huh?

60
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:26,100
Ah?

61
00:04:26,640 --> 00:04:28,980
[LUCA] This is mine.
Try to get in touch.

62
00:04:29,350 --> 00:04:31,350
[♪ cheerful music]

63
00:04:36,530 --> 00:04:37,690
[mysterious whoosh]

64
00:04:38,530 --> 00:04:39,610
[gasps]

65
00:04:40,400 --> 00:04:42,530
[♪ cheerful music continues]

66
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:45,620
[gasps]

67
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:51,370
[sighs]

68
00:04:56,630 --> 00:04:58,340
What a strange handsome guy.

69
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:01,220
-Mari, what do I do?
-Umm...

70
00:05:02,970 --> 00:05:04,430
Here, you can use this.

71
00:05:05,930 --> 00:05:07,310
It's my dad's old phone.

72
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:09,390
[both hum]

73
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:10,480
What's wrong?

74
00:05:11,770 --> 00:05:14,730
I won't allow a mermaid and
a human to fall in love.

75
00:05:16,020 --> 00:05:16,980
I wonder...

76
00:05:17,730 --> 00:05:19,650
Is this really the best
way I could be

77
00:05:19,780 --> 00:05:21,320
looking for my potential prince?

78
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:22,530
[WITCH] Hmm...

79
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:25,530
I don't know what Lisa
told you exactly, but

80
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:29,200
the only way to bring
the light back to your family

81
00:05:29,330 --> 00:05:31,370
is to find true love.

82
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:34,330
But only with... a human.

83
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,750
Hmm, but...

84
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:38,920
Do you want to send a message?

85
00:05:40,210 --> 00:05:42,590
Just tap here and speak,
and it'll write what you say.

86
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:44,180
[LARA] Lara.

87
00:05:44,300 --> 00:05:45,970
TODAY
LARA

88
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:48,970
-Yeah, there you go.
-So then what do I do next?

89
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:51,350
LARA
WHAT SHOULD I DO NEXT?

90
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,310
Huh?

91
00:05:52,440 --> 00:05:53,850
-No, your finger!
-Huh?

92
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:54,810
Huh?

93
00:05:55,350 --> 00:05:56,610
[beeps]
[gasps]

94
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:58,820
Hey, let's meet up.

95
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:00,940
LUCA
COME SEE ME.

96
00:06:01,070 --> 00:06:03,700
[MARI] Meeting up, just the two
of you? That's a date!

97
00:06:04,110 --> 00:06:05,240
IT'S A DATE.

98
00:06:05,370 --> 00:06:07,660
Oh no, take your
finger off, hurry!

99
00:06:08,290 --> 00:06:09,580
Oh, what should I do?

100
00:06:09,950 --> 00:06:11,040
Here!

101
00:06:13,670 --> 00:06:17,290
This Saturday at 10 AM, the
terrace at Lake Biwa.

102
00:06:20,590 --> 00:06:22,300
[BOTH] What?!

103
00:06:23,590 --> 00:06:26,300
[children shouting]

104
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:28,060
Oh, hello!

105
00:06:28,510 --> 00:06:30,260
It's good to see you.

106
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:35,980
[LUCA] This way.
[Lara gasps]

107
00:06:38,690 --> 00:06:41,320
So where... where are we going?

108
00:06:43,240 --> 00:06:44,530
[WOMAN] Also at the summit,

109
00:06:45,030 --> 00:06:46,910
you will experience
breathtaking -—

110
00:06:47,030 --> 00:06:48,870
-...fun, dear.
-Yeah!

111
00:06:48,990 --> 00:06:51,450
[Lara gasping and screaming]

112
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,290
[Lara pants]

113
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:58,500
Why are we so
high up a mountain?

114
00:06:59,540 --> 00:07:01,550
They said it was going to
be sunny today.

115
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:05,090
-We should go higher up.
-[gasps]

116
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:09,510
[indistinct chatter]

117
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:11,560
I wonder how she is.

118
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:14,730
-Alright, let's get started.
-[ALL] Right!

119
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:19,020
[LUCA] It's okay.
We'll be there soon.

120
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:22,570
[LARA] Who are you?
What do you do?

121
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,280
I go to school.

122
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:26,240
[LARA] And outside school?

123
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:29,740
-I do all sorts, I guess.
-All sorts?

124
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:34,700
-Having fun riding the lift?
-Having fun?

125
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:38,380
I guess, but where are we going?

126
00:07:39,080 --> 00:07:40,960
The view up there
is really beautiful.

127
00:07:41,380 --> 00:07:43,420
So then you like
beautiful views?

128
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:45,420
Yeah, I suppose.

129
00:07:46,630 --> 00:07:49,010
I like beautiful things, yes.

130
00:07:51,470 --> 00:07:53,010
[LARA] Beautiful things?

131
00:07:54,430 --> 00:07:57,730
You're disgusting with
that ugly, hideous form!

132
00:07:59,230 --> 00:08:00,230
[gasps]

133
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:07,650
I mean, when I say beautiful,
it comes in many forms.

134
00:08:09,070 --> 00:08:10,950
Let's talk about it
some other time.

135
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:17,160
We'll be there soon.
I hope you'll like the view.

136
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,330
[eerie whoosh]

137
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:29,380
The weather forecast
is totally off.

138
00:08:32,930 --> 00:08:33,970
[gasps]

139
00:08:36,310 --> 00:08:38,560
[wind howls]

140
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:45,570
[gasps]

141
00:08:45,940 --> 00:08:47,740
[wind howls]

142
00:08:52,030 --> 00:08:53,280
Thanks for your patience.

143
00:08:53,780 --> 00:08:56,080
You're waiting on 2 curry
buns, is that right?

144
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:58,160
Thank you.

145
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,080
I see now.

146
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,130
You're not really that
person, are you?

147
00:09:04,170 --> 00:09:05,130
[Luca gasps]

148
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:06,460
[LARA] Ah!

149
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:07,920
Are you okay?

150
00:09:08,220 --> 00:09:09,260
[Luca groans]

151
00:09:09,920 --> 00:09:11,010
Thank goodness!

152
00:09:11,470 --> 00:09:13,010
The food's okay!

153
00:09:14,850 --> 00:09:17,060
I'm starving, so I'm
glad you saved them.

154
00:09:18,270 --> 00:09:20,810
Wait! Both of them? Aren't
you going to share them?

155
00:09:21,270 --> 00:09:24,150
Apparently, this is what
they call a date.

156
00:09:25,150 --> 00:09:27,190
To be honest, I didn't
really understand it,

157
00:09:28,110 --> 00:09:30,070
but for some reason,
from that day on,

158
00:09:31,070 --> 00:09:33,200
Luca started getting
in touch with me.

159
00:09:35,370 --> 00:09:36,870
DONE WITH SCHOOL

160
00:09:36,990 --> 00:09:39,830
ARE YOU WORKING TODAY?

161
00:09:39,950 --> 00:09:41,790
CAN I SEE YOU?

162
00:09:41,910 --> 00:09:43,830
JUST FINISHED.

163
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:45,170
BE RIGHT THERE.

164
00:09:45,840 --> 00:09:48,420
[♪ cheerful music]

165
00:09:56,930 --> 00:09:59,310
YESTERDAY WAS FUN.

166
00:09:59,430 --> 00:10:02,310
I'LL SEND YOU THE
BIWAKO TERRACE PICS LATER.

167
00:10:02,430 --> 00:10:05,360
THANKS.

168
00:10:05,480 --> 00:10:07,440
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

169
00:10:07,570 --> 00:10:10,030
THE LAUNDRY.

170
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:12,200
I BROUGHT SOME SNACKS
FOR YOU FROM KYOTO.

171
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:14,030
I'LL BE RIGHT OVER.

172
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:22,540
[♪ cheerful music ends]

173
00:10:23,210 --> 00:10:25,620
GOOD NIGHT, LARA.

174
00:10:25,750 --> 00:10:28,380
Maybe he can't sleep
until he says good night.

175
00:10:29,210 --> 00:10:31,710
So come on, tell me,
what do you think of Luca?

176
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:33,550
Oh well,

177
00:10:36,550 --> 00:10:38,390
at first I was scared,

178
00:10:39,390 --> 00:10:40,350
but...

179
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:44,680
now I feel like he's somehow
different from that guy.

180
00:10:45,600 --> 00:10:46,640
[MARI] Hmm.

181
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:48,520
Huh?

182
00:10:49,230 --> 00:10:52,820
THERE'S A PLACE I WANT
TO SHOW YOU NEXT TIME.

183
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:57,280
I must confess, you're the first
person I've ever brought here.

184
00:10:57,490 --> 00:10:58,580
Oh.

185
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:02,250
It's a secret place. Even my
friends haven't been here.

186
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:08,040
And I'm only showing this
place to you and nobody else.

187
00:11:08,170 --> 00:11:09,170
Okay.

188
00:11:12,590 --> 00:11:13,510
[gasps]

189
00:11:13,920 --> 00:11:15,050
[LEO] Oh wow!

190
00:11:15,170 --> 00:11:16,180
Leo.

191
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:18,510
I told you not to
come over here.

192
00:11:18,930 --> 00:11:20,300
So it really is a girl.

193
00:11:21,470 --> 00:11:24,270
My name's Leo. Can you
tell me your name, please?

194
00:11:25,100 --> 00:11:26,060
I'm Lara.

195
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:27,600
[LEO] You are so cute!

196
00:11:28,150 --> 00:11:30,020
You're way too good
for my brother.

197
00:11:30,270 --> 00:11:32,190
Huh?

198
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:33,690
You might think my brother is
good-looking, but be warned

199
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:35,360
he's also pretty
clueless as well.

200
00:11:35,610 --> 00:11:37,280
-[LUCA] Leo.
-Yes, bro.

201
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:38,990
His paintings are terrible too.

202
00:11:39,570 --> 00:11:41,330
Bye, Lara.
Don't hold back.

203
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:42,830
Tell him they're terrible.

204
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,250
It really is for his own good.

205
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,500
They're not that terrible.

206
00:11:50,210 --> 00:11:51,790
[LARA] So did you paint that?

207
00:11:53,670 --> 00:11:55,130
What is this place?

208
00:11:57,170 --> 00:11:59,430
I wanted to show you this room.

209
00:11:59,930 --> 00:12:01,010
Huh?

210
00:12:08,350 --> 00:12:11,690
[♪ soft guitar music]

211
00:12:17,240 --> 00:12:18,990
What a mysterious room.

212
00:12:22,330 --> 00:12:23,240
Is this-—

213
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:26,290
-What is this exactly?
-This guy.

214
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:29,790
-Oh, and this?
-A wet dog.

215
00:12:31,210 --> 00:12:33,710
-What's this one?
-That's the real me.

216
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:38,010
Oh, but then is that
how you see yourself?

217
00:12:39,220 --> 00:12:40,220
The thing is,

218
00:12:41,180 --> 00:12:43,640
yes, I have a fondness for
beauty, but that doesn't always

219
00:12:43,760 --> 00:12:45,930
refer to things you
can see with your eyes.

220
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:50,350
True beauty comes from the
heart. It's to be discovered

221
00:12:50,690 --> 00:12:51,610
and felt.

222
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,610
I need to paint it and
preserve that beauty.

223
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:56,980
[wind howls]

224
00:12:57,110 --> 00:12:58,110
So...

225
00:12:58,450 --> 00:12:59,950
the very first moment I saw you,

226
00:13:00,450 --> 00:13:02,200
I wanted to paint you, Lara.

227
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:07,160
And then, I wanted to
discover more and more

228
00:13:07,700 --> 00:13:10,710
of your radiant and
unmistakable beauty.

229
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:16,460
I think you're
incredibly beautiful.

230
00:13:18,050 --> 00:13:19,010
And that's why.

231
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:20,300
[gasps]

232
00:13:20,880 --> 00:13:23,340
[♪ soft guitar music]

233
00:13:24,470 --> 00:13:25,510
Lara...

234
00:13:27,600 --> 00:13:29,810
I wanted you to see what I see.

235
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:33,230
[♪ soft guitar music continues]

236
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:38,690
[Lara laughs]

237
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:48,160
What-— what's so funny?!

238
00:13:49,620 --> 00:13:50,580
So sorry.

239
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:52,250
Then why are you laughing?

240
00:13:52,710 --> 00:13:55,380
I mean, I've never seen
anything like it.

241
00:13:55,710 --> 00:13:57,670
Well, I've just not
finished it yet.

242
00:13:58,090 --> 00:13:59,880
I do think it's a good painting.

243
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,260
Well, you know,
I need to add more colors.

244
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:08,220
[gasps]

245
00:14:08,970 --> 00:14:11,430
[eerie whoosh]

246
00:14:15,610 --> 00:14:16,610
[gasps]

247
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:24,360
[Lara pants]

248
00:14:36,130 --> 00:14:37,710
[Luca pants]

249
00:14:41,550 --> 00:14:46,130
-What happened back there?
-[LARA] That-— that dagger.

250
00:14:47,260 --> 00:14:49,640
-Lara?
-I'm sorry.

251
00:14:51,010 --> 00:14:52,770
I just need to be left
alone right now.

252
00:14:55,140 --> 00:14:57,060
Lara! Please come back soon!

253
00:14:58,060 --> 00:15:00,320
I-— I would like to
finish the painting.

254
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,450
Welcome back.
You're pretty late.

255
00:15:06,320 --> 00:15:08,490
So, how was it?
Huh?

256
00:15:13,330 --> 00:15:16,210
ARE YOU OKAY?

257
00:15:16,420 --> 00:15:19,710
I WANT TO SEE YOU AGAIN.

258
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:23,340
SORRY.

259
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:25,090
I'LL CHECK IN AGAIN.

260
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:26,220
Hmm.

261
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:30,140
GOOD NIGHT.

262
00:15:32,060 --> 00:15:35,020
[LISA] So then, the witch
has already noticed us.

263
00:15:36,440 --> 00:15:39,440
If we try to get close to Lara,
she'll surely drive us away.

264
00:15:40,110 --> 00:15:41,690
-So, let's just go there and-—
-No.

265
00:15:42,650 --> 00:15:43,740
There's another way.

266
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:47,150
I'll get Lara back no
matter what it takes

267
00:15:48,070 --> 00:15:49,700
before it's too
late for all of us.

268
00:15:52,330 --> 00:15:55,040
I don't want this, so you can
have my portion.

269
00:15:56,460 --> 00:15:58,000
-Lara?
-No, thanks. I'm good.

270
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,750
-[MARI] Uh...
-[YOSHIYA] Hmm?

271
00:16:02,920 --> 00:16:04,170
Fireworks show is next week.

272
00:16:04,880 --> 00:16:06,470
[BOY] That's right!
Shall we go?

273
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:09,590
-Going with that girl, Luca?
-Nope.

274
00:16:10,550 --> 00:16:12,470
How many girlfriends have
you had now?

275
00:16:13,810 --> 00:16:14,890
Zero.

276
00:16:15,020 --> 00:16:16,430
Must be someone you like, right?

277
00:16:17,890 --> 00:16:20,060
[alarm beeping]

278
00:16:21,190 --> 00:16:22,020
[beeping]

279
00:16:22,150 --> 00:16:23,070
[sighs]

280
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:25,190
CAN I CALL YOU TONIGHT?

281
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:32,160
[LISA] Only when the chosen
princess feels pure, true love

282
00:16:33,330 --> 00:16:36,200
does a radiant light shine
from the depths of her heart.

283
00:16:36,330 --> 00:16:37,870
[magic sound]

284
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,420
[LARA] I've fallen in love
with a human.

285
00:16:41,130 --> 00:16:42,590
I've fallen in love with you.

286
00:16:44,130 --> 00:16:45,000
[gasps]

287
00:16:45,130 --> 00:16:48,380
[♪ ethereal music]

288
00:16:57,310 --> 00:17:00,230
[DAGGER] Tell me, why are
you rejecting me?

289
00:17:01,860 --> 00:17:02,690
[LARA] What?

290
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:04,860
Tell me,

291
00:17:05,400 --> 00:17:06,690
why won't you love me?

292
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:10,610
[LARA] Was that?
The dagger?

293
00:17:13,410 --> 00:17:17,160
I want to devour...
that soul of yours.

294
00:17:17,410 --> 00:17:18,500
[gasps]

295
00:17:19,870 --> 00:17:21,210
I want to pierce it...

296
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,380
the prince's heart.

297
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:28,260
I want to devour.

298
00:17:29,210 --> 00:17:30,420
I want to devour!

299
00:17:30,920 --> 00:17:32,300
I want to devour!

300
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:41,230
[♪ tense music]

301
00:17:46,520 --> 00:17:48,440
[LARA] I had completely
forgotten.

302
00:17:49,230 --> 00:17:50,150
That day,

303
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:52,860
the pure light of love
within my heart

304
00:17:53,490 --> 00:17:55,320
transformed into a blade.

305
00:17:56,990 --> 00:18:00,370
That light from my heart,
it should be born out of love.

306
00:18:00,910 --> 00:18:01,960
So why?

307
00:18:02,410 --> 00:18:03,500
I'm not sure.

308
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:05,000
But...

309
00:18:05,130 --> 00:18:06,170
[magical sound]

310
00:18:07,170 --> 00:18:09,300
if this thing is supposed
to be my heart,

311
00:18:10,550 --> 00:18:14,300
then it might end up hurting
someone, or even worse.

312
00:18:17,010 --> 00:18:18,180
Does that bother you?

313
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:21,390
Come on, you're worried too.

314
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:24,310
I just thought that maybe...

315
00:18:25,310 --> 00:18:27,230
she'd finally met her prince.

316
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:30,650
What's that?

317
00:18:31,650 --> 00:18:33,700
[MARI] Let me guess, you've
never seen fireworks?

318
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:35,030
Huh?

319
00:18:35,490 --> 00:18:38,120
I watch it here with my
family every single year.

320
00:18:38,370 --> 00:18:39,410
I see.

321
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:43,250
Some people go with friends,
and some with close friends.

322
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:48,290
Would you like to
go with anyone?

323
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:53,170
So... do you want to
come this year then?

324
00:18:56,130 --> 00:18:57,640
You seem a little
down lately, bro.

325
00:18:58,350 --> 00:19:00,140
Did Lara dump you or somethi-—?
Huh?

326
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,140
[sighs]

327
00:19:08,270 --> 00:19:10,650
[panting]

328
00:19:19,030 --> 00:19:21,370
[♪ soft guitar music]

329
00:19:24,870 --> 00:19:25,710
[MARI] Lara!

330
00:19:26,330 --> 00:19:27,290
Mari.

331
00:19:28,330 --> 00:19:31,000
Luca, he was just standing
at the overpass crying.

332
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:33,090
I can't see him anymore.

333
00:19:34,380 --> 00:19:37,510
-You can't leave it like this.
-This is the only way.

334
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:44,220
So you're just going to walk
away and leave him like that?

335
00:19:48,480 --> 00:19:50,190
-A-—
-No, Mari. You're right.

336
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:53,780
I'll go and end it properly.

337
00:19:58,990 --> 00:20:00,030
[LARA] Luca!

338
00:20:03,120 --> 00:20:04,160
Lara! I-—

339
00:20:08,170 --> 00:20:10,080
Have you been waiting
here all along?

340
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:11,960
I don't know.

341
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:15,380
[LARA] So why are you
making that long face?

342
00:20:18,090 --> 00:20:20,300
Did you really want to
paint me that much?

343
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:24,020
Is it because I'm a mermaid?

344
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,100
Uh.

345
00:20:29,100 --> 00:20:31,360
Getting close to somebody
like me isn't the

346
00:20:31,480 --> 00:20:33,480
same as getting close
to another human.

347
00:20:34,570 --> 00:20:35,610
[sighs]

348
00:20:36,570 --> 00:20:37,610
I'm sorry.

349
00:20:40,030 --> 00:20:43,280
I-— I can't see you anymore!

350
00:20:45,200 --> 00:20:47,370
[♪ soft guitar music]

351
00:20:49,620 --> 00:20:50,670
I see.

352
00:20:52,210 --> 00:20:53,340
I understand.

353
00:20:54,340 --> 00:20:55,340
[sighs]

354
00:20:58,720 --> 00:21:00,470
[♪ soft guitar music]

355
00:21:00,930 --> 00:21:01,760
[thud]

356
00:21:02,100 --> 00:21:03,260
[gasps]

357
00:21:04,140 --> 00:21:06,470
[♪ soft guitar music continues]

358
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:11,100
Luca?

359
00:21:18,610 --> 00:21:21,360
At first I was interested
because you were a mermaid,

360
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:24,410
but now... that's all changed.

361
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:30,410
And I know, even though you
don't like me because I'm human,

362
00:21:33,080 --> 00:21:36,050
and that you don't want
to see me anymore, I'm-—

363
00:21:37,420 --> 00:21:39,510
sorry, Lara.

364
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:43,180
I like you because you're you.

365
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:45,680
[sighs]

366
00:21:55,520 --> 00:21:56,650
[LARA] Maybe,

367
00:21:57,610 --> 00:22:00,570
I've been waiting to
hear those words

368
00:22:01,440 --> 00:22:02,740
my entire life.

369
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:06,370
Thank you.

370
00:22:13,290 --> 00:22:15,040
[♪ closing music begins]

371
00:22:24,300 --> 00:22:26,010
Translation: Sachiko Takahashi

372
00:22:26,140 --> 00:22:27,310
Timing: Andy Ellis

373
00:22:27,430 --> 00:22:29,270
Editing and Typesetting:
Ashley Barboza

374
00:22:29,390 --> 00:22:30,600
Quality Control: Riley Dalton

375
00:22:30,720 --> 00:22:32,520
Translation Check:
Sriram Gurunathan

376
00:23:18,860 --> 00:23:19,520
I know now.

377
00:23:20,400 --> 00:23:23,570
I want to get closer
to this person!

378
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:42,500
[♪ closing music ends]

379
00:23:46,630 --> 00:23:48,340
- [LARA] We're home!
- [MARI] Hey!

380
00:23:48,470 --> 00:23:50,850
-[MAKOTO] Ah, Lara!
-You're home late.

381
00:23:50,970 --> 00:23:52,600
Weren't the fireworks
just wonderful?

382
00:23:53,060 --> 00:23:54,060
Yeah, they always are.

383
00:23:54,350 --> 00:23:55,430
[chuckles]

384
00:23:57,640 --> 00:24:00,020
TO BE CONTINUED

